#
# Counter-example for the `math:` expression lowering
# (crates/logic/src/physical/lower.rs, MathLoweringError::ExpressionDepthExceeded): a
# chain of 501 nested math:ApplicationExpression nodes (n0 the root, each naming the
# next as its sole operand through math:argumentSlot/math:slotExpression), one level
# deeper than MAX_MATH_EXPRESSION_DEPTH (500) in crates/logic/src/physical/lower.rs —
# the mutual recursion `lower_math_node` walks an authored RDF graph with no acyclicity
# or depth guarantee from the type system, so a pathologically deep authoring is
# rejected as a typed, catchable error rather than an unbounded stack dive. n501 (the
# innermost slot target) is never even dereferenced: the depth guard fires on ENTRY to
# `lower_math_node` for n501, before any type dispatch, so it need not exist. The
# authored math:structuralKey on the root (n0) lets the reasoned-graph gate
# (check_structural_key_on_rejected_expression) also reach it.
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:n0 a math:ApplicationExpression ;
    math:operator ex:op ;
    math:argumentSlot ex:s0 ;
    math:structuralKey "not-a-real-digest" .
ex:s0 a math:ArgumentSlot ; math:slotIndex 0 ; math:slotExpression ex:n1 .
ex:n1 a math:ApplicationExpression ;
    math:operator ex:op ;
    math:argumentSlot ex:s1 .
ex:s1 a math:ArgumentSlot ; math:slotIndex 0 ; math:slotExpression ex:n2 .
ex:n2 a math:ApplicationExpression ;
    math:operator ex:op ;
    math:argumentSlot ex:s2 .
ex:s2 a math:ArgumentSlot ; math:slotIndex 0 ; math:slotExpression ex:n3 .
ex:n3 a math:ApplicationExpression ;
    math:operator ex:op ;
    math:argumentSlot ex:s3 .
